---
layout: base.njk
bodyClass: docs-home-page
---
{% from "install.njk" import siteLink %}
{#- The specimens below are declared once and used more than once: rendered
    live, and highlighted into the listing beside them. One string, so the
    markup a reader copies is the markup that produced what they are
    looking at.

    They are written flush to the left margin on purpose: whitespace inside a
    `set` block is captured verbatim, and this is the indentation that ends up
    in the <pre>. -#}

{#- The hero's specimen: the source slab and the rendered card in front of
    it are this one string. Written to fit a phone's code pane without a
    horizontal scrollbar: one attribute set per line, nothing optional. -#}
{%- set heroSpecimen -%}
<article>
  <h2>Sign in</h2>
  <form>
    <label>
      Email
      <input type="email" required>
    </label>
    <label>
      Password
      <input type="password" required>
    </label>
    <label>
      <input type="checkbox" checked>
      Remember me
    </label>
    <button>Sign in</button>
  </form>
</article>
{%- endset -%}



{#- The story's specimen: a train ticket, in elements the browser already
    knows how to run (dates and times, terms and values, a gauge with its
    own good and bad ranges, a disclosure, a button) and no class. Used
    three times, always the same string: listed, rendered with no
    stylesheet at all, and rendered by Cirth. -#}
{%- set storySpecimen -%}
<article>
  <hgroup>
    <h3>Lisbon to Porto</h3>
    <p>Alfa Pendular, <time datetime="2026-11-12T08:39">12 Nov, 08:39</time></p>
  </hgroup>
  <dl>
    <dt>Coach and seat</dt>
    <dd>5, seat 42 (window)</dd>
    <dt>Arrives</dt>
    <dd><time datetime="2026-11-12T11:28">11:28</time>, Porto Campanhã</dd>
  </dl>
  <label>
    Coach 5 is 70% full
    <meter value="0.7" low="0.5" high="0.8" optimum="0">70%</meter>
  </label>
  <details>
    <summary>Change or cancel</summary>
    <p>Free changes until 08:09.</p>
  </details>
  <button type="button">Show ticket</button>
</article>
{%- endset %}
{%- set storyStats = storySpecimen | markupStats %}

{#- The presets comparator's specimen: a field, two switches and two
    actions, laid across the whole width (presetCopy below), so whichever
    side of the divider the reader looks at holds the accent and a corner. -#}
{%- set presetSpecimen -%}
<article>
  <label>
    Email
    <input type="email" value="ada@example.com">
  </label>
  <fieldset>
    <legend>Email me about</legend>
    <label>
      <input type="checkbox" role="switch" checked>
      Product news
    </label>
    <label>
      <input type="checkbox" role="switch" checked>
      Weekly digest
    </label>
  </fieldset>
  <footer>
    <button type="button" class="secondary">Cancel</button>
    <button type="button">Save</button>
  </footer>
</article>
{%- endset -%}

{#- The theme demonstration's specimen: a project's launch card, whose bar
    and button take the accent, whose corners take the radius and which
    stands on the canvas, so each of the three declarations has something
    to change. -#}
{%- set themeSpecimen -%}
<article>
  <hgroup>
    <h3>Atlas 2.0 launch</h3>
    <p>On track for <time datetime="2026-11-12">12 November</time></p>
  </hgroup>
  <label>
    Launch checklist, 18 of 24
    <progress value="18" max="24"></progress>
  </label>
  <dl>
    <dt>Owner</dt>
    <dd>Ada Lovelace</dd>
  </dl>
  <details>
    <summary>2 blockers</summary>
    <p>Billing emails in Safari, and the CSV export.</p>
  </details>
  <button type="button">Ship it</button>
</article>
{%- endset %}

{#- A copy of Cirth that is only this copy's: the scoped build in a
    declarative shadow root, so the page's preset and theme do not reach
    it and it renders with no script. Its scheme is set on the `.cirth`
    root inside the shadow tree, never on the host: a `data-theme` on the
    host of a shadow root leaves the copy without its tokens. Every preset
    is loaded and switched off with `media`; the comparator's script turns
    one on, in both copies at once, so a change of preset fetches nothing
    and never paints a half without its theme. -#}
{%- macro presetCopy(markup, scheme) -%}
<template shadowrootmode="open"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/generated/cirth-lab-scoped.css">{% for preset in presets %}<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/generated/presets/{{ preset.name }}.css" media="not all" data-docs-preset="{{ preset.name }}">{% endfor %}<style>:host{display:block}.cirth{position:relative;box-sizing:border-box;min-block-size:100%;padding:3rem clamp(1rem,3vw,2rem) clamp(1rem,3vw,2rem);background:var(--cirth-canvas)}.cirth>article{margin:0}.cirth fieldset{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));column-gap:1rem}.cirth fieldset>legend{grid-column:1/-1}.cirth fieldset>label{margin-block:0}.cirth article>footer{display:flex;justify-content:space-between}@media (width<30rem){.cirth fieldset{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}}.scheme{position:absolute;inset-block-start:1rem;margin:0;color:var(--cirth-muted-color);font-size:var(--cirth-meta-font-size);font-weight:var(--cirth-font-weight-medium)}.scheme-light{inset-inline-start:clamp(1rem,3vw,2rem)}.scheme-dark{inset-inline-end:clamp(1rem,3vw,2rem)}</style><div class="cirth" data-theme="{{ scheme }}" data-docs-compare-surface><p class="scheme scheme-{{ scheme }}">{{ "Light" if scheme == "light" else "Dark" }}</p>{{ markup | safe }}</div></template>
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- The theme demonstration's copy: the scoped build, and each state's
    three declarations as a stylesheet switched off with `media`, the last
    one on, so with no script the copy shows the finished theme. The
    controller turns on the state the scroll has reached. The copy follows
    the page's scheme from inside its shadow root (see presetCopy). -#}
{%- macro themeCopy(markup) -%}
<template shadowrootmode="open"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/generated/cirth-lab-scoped.css">{% for state in themeDemo.states %}<style media="{{ 'all' if loop.last else 'not all' }}" data-docs-theme-state="{{ state.id }}">{{ state.css }}</style>{% endfor %}<style>:host{display:block}.cirth{box-sizing:border-box;display:grid;place-items:center;min-block-size:100%;padding:clamp(1.25rem,4vw,3rem);background:var(--cirth-canvas)}.cirth>article{inline-size:min(100%,26rem);margin:0}</style><div class="cirth" data-docs-theme-surface>{{ markup | safe }}</div></template>
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- The marks' places in the framework band: two rings round one centre,
    six on the inner, ten on the outer, in the order frameworks.js
    features them. A place is a ring and an angle; the stylesheet turns
    it into a position, and the inner ring's marks are the larger. -#}
{%- set orbitSlots = [
  { ring: "inner", at: 300 }, { ring: "outer", at: 0 }, { ring: "outer", at: 36 },
  { ring: "inner", at: 0 }, { ring: "outer", at: 72 }, { ring: "outer", at: 108 },
  { ring: "inner", at: 60 }, { ring: "outer", at: 144 }, { ring: "outer", at: 180 },
  { ring: "inner", at: 120 }, { ring: "outer", at: 216 }, { ring: "outer", at: 252 },
  { ring: "inner", at: 180 }, { ring: "outer", at: 288 }, { ring: "inner", at: 240 },
  { ring: "outer", at: 324 }
] -%}


<main id="main-content" class="docs-home" data-pagefind-body>
	{#- The field of colour behind the whole page: one fixed layer of three
	    soft glows from the accent, which the motion script moves, scales,
	    fades and turns as the scenes go by, so the page has one field that
	    travels rather than a gradient per section. With no script and under
	    reduced motion it holds the hero's arrangement. Decoration only. -#}
	<div class="docs-aurora" aria-hidden="true"><span class="docs-aurora-warm"></span><span class="docs-aurora-cool"></span><span class="docs-aurora-gold"></span></div>

	{#- 1. The hero. Copy first in the document and on every screen; the
	    demo is a source slab with the card it renders laid over it, offset
	    so both read at once. The card is rendered by the page's own Cirth,
	    not a screenshot, and is inert: it is a picture of the output, not a
	    form on the home page. The field of colour behind it is the page's
	    shared one (.docs-aurora, above), in its hero arrangement, and no
	    text sits on its brightest part. -#}
	<section class="docs-hero" aria-labelledby="home-title">
		<div class="docs-home-inner docs-hero-grid">
			<div class="docs-hero-copy">
				<h1 id="home-title">Semantic HTML in.<br />Finished UI out.</h1>
				<p class="docs-hero-lede">{{ hero.tagline }}</p>
				<p class="docs-hero-actions">
					{% for action in hero.actions %}
						<a href="{{ action.link }}" role="button"{% if action.theme != "brand" %} class="secondary outline"{% endif %}>{{ action.text }}</a>
					{% endfor %}
				</p>
				<div class="docs-hero-install">
					<p id="hero-install-label">Install from npm</p>
					<pre tabindex="0" aria-labelledby="hero-install-label"><code class="hljs language-sh">npm install @cirthcss/cirth</code></pre>
				</div>
			</div>
			<figure class="docs-hero-demo" aria-labelledby="hero-demo-caption">
				<div class="docs-hero-stack">
					<div class="docs-hero-source">
						<p class="docs-pane-label" aria-hidden="true"><code>sign-in.html</code></p>
						<pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Source of the sign-in card"><code class="hljs language-html">{{ heroSpecimen | highlight | safe }}</code></pre>
					</div>
					<div class="docs-hero-render" inert>{{ heroSpecimen | safe }}</div>
				</div>
				<figcaption id="hero-demo-caption">The markup on the left is the whole source of the card in front of it. No class, no script.</figcaption>
			</figure>
		</div>
	</section>

	{#- 2. The facts, as one ruled band rather than four boxes. Each is a
	    number from this build or a property the project treats a break of
	    as a bug, and each links to where it can be checked. -#}
	<section class="docs-facts-band" aria-labelledby="facts-title">
		<div class="docs-home-inner">
			<h2 id="facts-title" class="sr-only">At a glance</h2>
			<dl class="docs-fact-list">
				<div data-reveal>
					<dt>JavaScript runtime</dt>
					<dd><strong>0 B</strong> <a href="/why-cirth#pure-css-nothing-to-run">Nothing to run</a></dd>
				</div>
				<div data-reveal>
					<dt>Default build, gzipped</dt>
					<dd><strong>{{ proof.size.label if proof.size else "About 15 KB" }}</strong> <a href="/about#size-and-what-it-is-a-budget-for">Measured on every build</a></dd>
				</div>
				<div data-reveal>
					<dt>Accessibility baseline</dt>
					<dd><strong>WCAG 2.2 AA</strong> <a href="/guides/accessibility#the-baseline">How it is audited</a></dd>
				</div>
				<div data-reveal>
					<dt>Stacks</dt>
					<dd><strong>Any</strong> <a href="/installation#guides">{{ frameworks.guides.length }} checked guides</a></dd>
				</div>
			</dl>
		</div>
	</section>

	{#- 3. The story: what the reader writes, what the browser already does
	    with it, and what Cirth adds, told in three steps beside one stage.
	    In the document the steps and their pictures alternate (text,
	    picture, text, picture), which is the order a phone, a short window,
	    a reader with reduced motion and a page with no script get: three
	    blocks, everything complete. On a wide, tall screen with a script,
	    the section is a long scroll with the stage held in view: the
	    markup is typed as the reader scrolls (a picture of it: the listing
	    itself is always whole in the document), then the browser's own
	    rendering comes up in front of it, then the same markup with Cirth
	    replaces it. Everything follows the scroll position, both ways, and
	    nothing moves while the reader does not. The browser's rendering is
	    the markup in a shadow root with no stylesheet at all: `all:
	    initial` resets what the page would hand it by inheritance, and
	    WebKit keeps the inherited face through it, so the standard face,
	    serif, is named as well. -#}
	<section class="docs-story" aria-labelledby="story-title" data-docs-story data-aurora="story">
		<div class="docs-story-scene">
			<div class="docs-home-inner docs-story-grid">
				<header class="docs-story-head" data-reveal>
					<h2 id="story-title">Built on HTML, not around it.</h2>
					<p>You write the element, the browser gives it its behaviour, and Cirth gives it its look. Nothing is replaced on the way.</p>
				</header>
				<div class="docs-story-step" data-docs-story-step="1" data-reveal>
					<h3><span class="docs-story-number" aria-hidden="true">1</span> Write the element</h3>
					<p><code>&lt;time&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;dl&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;meter&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;details&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;button&gt;</code>: each one says what it is, so nothing else has to. No class, no wrapper, no script.</p>
				</div>
				<figure class="docs-story-part docs-story-source" data-docs-story-part="1" data-reveal>
					<pre tabindex="0" aria-label="The markup of the ticket"><code class="hljs language-html" data-docs-story-code>{{ storySpecimen | highlight | safe }}</code><code class="hljs language-html docs-story-typed" aria-hidden="true" data-docs-story-typed></code></pre>
					<figcaption>The markup, as you write it</figcaption>
				</figure>
				<div class="docs-story-step" data-docs-story-step="2" data-reveal>
					<h3><span class="docs-story-number" aria-hidden="true">2</span> The browser brings the behaviour</h3>
					<p>It reads the times, pairs each term with its value, colours the gauge by its own good and bad ranges, opens and closes the disclosure and moves focus with the keyboard. Unstyled, it already works.</p>
				</div>
				<figure class="docs-story-part docs-story-browser" data-docs-story-part="2" data-reveal>
					<div class="docs-story-ua" inert><template shadowrootmode="open"><style>:host{display:block}.ua{all:initial;font-family:serif;display:block;color-scheme:light;background:Canvas;color:CanvasText;padding:1rem;box-sizing:border-box}</style><div class="ua">{{ storySpecimen | safe }}</div></template></div>
					<figcaption>The same markup in the browser, with no stylesheet</figcaption>
				</figure>
				<div class="docs-story-step" data-docs-story-step="3" data-reveal>
					<h3><span class="docs-story-number" aria-hidden="true">3</span> Cirth draws it</h3>
					<p>One stylesheet adds type, spacing, colour, focus and every state, in light and in dark. The markup has not changed. Open the disclosure.</p>
				</div>
				<figure class="docs-story-part docs-story-cirth" data-docs-story-part="3" data-reveal>
					<div class="docs-story-result">{{ storySpecimen | safe }}</div>
					<figcaption>The same markup, with Cirth</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	{#- 4. Measured, not promised: three figures, each read off the thing it
	    is about. The classes are counted in the ticket above, the scripts
	    in the package's dist/, the size off the default build. Each says
	    what it was measured on. A wide screen holds the three in view and
	    brings them up one after another with the scroll; everywhere else
	    they are simply there. -#}
	<section class="docs-measured" aria-labelledby="measured-title" data-docs-measured data-aurora="measured">
		<div class="docs-measured-scene">
			<div class="docs-home-inner docs-measured-grid">
				<header class="docs-measured-head" data-reveal>
					<h2 id="measured-title">Less markup. Nothing to run.</h2>
					<p>Three figures, each measured on the thing it describes, not estimated against anything else.</p>
				</header>
				<ol class="docs-measured-list">
					<li class="docs-measured-fact" data-docs-measured-fact="1" data-reveal>
						<p class="docs-measured-figure"><strong>{{ storyStats.classes }}</strong> <span>classes</span></p>
						<div class="docs-measured-text">
							<p>In the ticket above: {{ storyStats.elements }} elements, and only the attributes that say what they mean.</p>
							<ul class="docs-measured-tags" aria-label="The elements of the ticket, in order">
								{%- for name in storyStats.names %}
								<li style="--docs-index: {{ loop.index0 }}"><code>{{ name }}</code></li>
								{%- endfor %}
							</ul>
						</div>
					</li>
					<li class="docs-measured-fact" data-docs-measured-fact="2" data-reveal>
						<p class="docs-measured-figure"><strong>{{ packageContents.scriptBytes if packageContents else 0 }}&nbsp;B</strong> <span>of JavaScript</span></p>
						<div class="docs-measured-text">
							<p>Cirth is compiled CSS. The package's <code>dist/</code> holds {{ packageContents.stylesheets if packageContents else "only" }} stylesheets and {{ packageContents.tokens if packageContents else "its" }} token files{% if packageContents %}, and {{ "no script" if packageContents.scripts == 0 else packageContents.scripts + " scripts" }}{% endif %}: nothing to load, hydrate or update.</p>
						</div>
					</li>
					<li class="docs-measured-fact" data-docs-measured-fact="3" data-reveal>
						<p class="docs-measured-figure"><strong>{{ proof.size.label if proof.size else "About 15 KB" }}</strong> <span>gzipped</span></p>
						<div class="docs-measured-text">
							<p>The default build, measured on every build of this site. The others, the same way:</p>
							{%- if packageContents and packageContents.builds.length %}
							<dl class="docs-measured-builds">
								{%- for build in packageContents.builds %}
								<div style="--docs-share: {{ build.share }}; --docs-index: {{ loop.index0 }}"><dt>{{ build.name }}</dt><dd>{{ build.label }}</dd></div>
								{%- endfor %}
							</dl>
							{%- endif %}
						</div>
					</li>
				</ol>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	{#- 5. Your theme: the same card, and three of Cirth's custom properties
	    changed one at a time as the reader scrolls (themeDemo.js). The
	    values are the demonstration's own, none of them a preset's. The
	    listing beside the form shows each declaration as it is at that
	    point and marks the one that just changed. With no script or with
	    reduced motion the finished theme is shown, with all three. -#}
	<section class="docs-theme" aria-labelledby="theme-title" data-docs-theme data-aurora="theme">
		<div class="docs-theme-scene">
			<div class="docs-home-inner docs-theme-grid">
				<header class="docs-theme-head" data-reveal>
					<h2 id="theme-title">Your theme. Same HTML.</h2>
					<p>Every colour, radius and surface is a <code>--cirth-*</code> custom property. Three of them change below, one at a time, and the markup of the card never does.</p>
				</header>
				<ol class="docs-theme-steps" data-reveal>
					{%- for state in themeDemo.states %}{% if state.changes %}
					<li data-docs-theme-step="{{ state.id }}"><span>{{ state.label }}</span> <code>{{ state.changes }}</code></li>
					{%- endif %}{% endfor %}
				</ol>
				<pre class="docs-theme-code" tabindex="0" aria-label="The three declarations" data-reveal><code class="hljs language-css"><span class="hljs-selector-pseudo">:root</span> {
{%- for token in themeDemo.tokens %}
<span class="docs-theme-line" data-docs-theme-token="{{ token }}">  <span class="hljs-attr">{{ token }}</span>: {% for state in themeDemo.states %}{% if loop.first or state.changes == token %}<span class="docs-theme-value" data-docs-theme-value="{{ state.id }}"{% if loop.first %} hidden{% endif %}>{{ state.values[token] }}</span>{% endif %}{% endfor %};</span>
{%- endfor %}
}</code></pre>
				<figure class="docs-theme-preview" data-reveal>
					<div class="docs-theme-copy" inert>{{ themeCopy(themeSpecimen) }}</div>
					<figcaption>The same card throughout, in its own copy of Cirth, so this page's theme and preset do not reach it.</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	{#- 6. Presets: one form in a preset's light and dark scheme, cut by a
	    divider. The list picks the preset both halves wear, and
	    the line under it is the import that loads it. The divider is a real
	    range input over the frame: a pointer, a finger and the arrow keys
	    all move it, and it has a name and a value. Both copies are inert
	    pictures. With no script the default theme shows, the divider rests
	    in the middle, and neither control is shown. -#}
	<section class="docs-presets" aria-labelledby="presets-title" data-aurora="presets">
		<div class="docs-home-inner docs-presets-grid">
			<header class="docs-presets-head" data-reveal>
				<h2 id="presets-title">Presets, light and dark.</h2>
				<p>Material, Metro and Plain are short files of tokens loaded after Cirth, and each has both schemes. Pick one, then move the divider.</p>
				<p class="docs-presets-pick" data-docs-compare-pick hidden>
					<label for="compare-preset">Preset</label>
					<select id="compare-preset" data-docs-compare-preset>
						{%- for state in themePreview.states %}
						<option value="{{ state.name }}">{{ state.short }}</option>
						{%- endfor %}
					</select>
				</p>
				<p class="docs-presets-import" data-docs-compare-imports>
					{%- for state in themePreview.states %}
					<code data-docs-compare-import="{{ state.name }}"{% if loop.first %} data-current{% endif %}>@import "@cirthcss/cirth{{ '' if state.name == 'default' else '/presets/' + state.name }}";</code>
					{%- endfor %}
				</p>
				<p class="docs-section-more"><a href="/presets">What each preset changes</a></p>
			</header>
			<figure class="docs-compare" data-docs-compare data-reveal>
				<div class="docs-compare-frame">
					<div class="docs-compare-layer docs-compare-light" inert>{{ presetCopy(presetSpecimen, "light") }}</div>
					<div class="docs-compare-layer docs-compare-dark" inert>{{ presetCopy(presetSpecimen, "dark") }}</div>
					<div class="docs-compare-divider" aria-hidden="true"><span class="docs-compare-handle"></span></div>
					<input class="docs-compare-range" type="range" min="0" max="100" step="1" value="50" aria-label="Divider between the light and the dark scheme" aria-describedby="compare-caption" aria-valuetext="Half light, half dark" data-docs-compare-range hidden>
				</div>
				<figcaption id="compare-caption">The same form twice, cut by a divider: the preset in its light scheme on the left, in its dark scheme on the right. Each half is its own copy of Cirth, so the theme and preset this page uses do not reach it.</figcaption>
			</figure>
		</div>
	</section>

	{#- 7. Framework agnostic. On the page's shared field of colour, the
	    marks orbit Cirth's own in two drawn rings, the rings behind them,
	    without a card each, at two sizes; they turn only as the reader
	    scrolls, stay upright, and hold still under the pointer or the
	    keyboard. On a phone and under reduced motion they stand still. Each
	    mark is a link to the project's own site, named as such; the way to
	    the guides is the one action. The marks are a fixed set from
	    frameworks.js, every one shown under its owner's terms. -#}
	<section class="docs-agnostic" aria-labelledby="agnostic-title" data-docs-agnostic data-aurora="agnostic">
		<div class="docs-home-inner docs-agnostic-grid">
			<div class="docs-agnostic-field">
				<span class="docs-agnostic-core" aria-hidden="true">
					<img class="docs-logo docs-logo-light" src="/logo_brand.svg" alt="" width="64" height="64" />
					<img class="docs-logo docs-logo-dark" src="/logo_brand_dark.svg" alt="" width="64" height="64" />
				</span>
				<ul class="docs-agnostic-orbit" aria-label="Projects with a guide">
					{%- for guide in frameworks.featured %}
					{%- set slot = orbitSlots[loop.index0] %}
					<li class="docs-agnostic-{{ slot.ring }}" style="--at: {{ slot.at }}deg">{{ siteLink(guide, 40 if slot.ring == "inner" else 30, "docs-agnostic-mark") }}</li>
					{%- endfor %}
				</ul>
			</div>
			<div class="docs-agnostic-copy" data-reveal>
				<h2 id="agnostic-title">Framework agnostic. Works everywhere.</h2>
				<p>Cirth styles HTML, so it does not mind what wrote it: a JavaScript framework, a server template, a CMS, a static site generator or a desktop app.</p>
				<p>Each guide shows where the one import goes in that stack, and the one setting that keeps a build from rewriting Cirth's colours.</p>
				<p class="docs-agnostic-actions"><a href="/installation#guides" role="button">Browse all {{ frameworks.count }} guides</a></p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	{#- 8. The close. -#}
	<section class="docs-pure" aria-labelledby="pure-title">
		<div class="docs-home-inner">
			<header class="docs-section-head" data-reveal>
				<h2 id="pure-title">Pure CSS. Whatever writes your HTML.</h2>
				<p>No runtime, no components, no build step of its own: one stylesheet from a CDN or from npm, and the HTML you already write is finished.</p>
				<p class="docs-hero-actions">
					<a href="/installation" role="button">Get started</a>
					<a href="/why-cirth" role="button" class="secondary outline">Why Cirth</a>
				</p>
			</header>
		</div>
	</section>
</main>

<script>
	// The home page's one motion controller. Everything it does follows the
	// scroll position: one passive scroll listener, at most one update per
	// animation frame, and the state of every scene computed from where the
	// page is now, never from where it has been, so a link to a fragment, a
	// reload half way down, the back button and scrolling backwards all land
	// on the right state. Nothing runs while the page is still. An
	// IntersectionObserver only says which scenes are near the window; no
	// effect has an observer or a timer of its own.
	//
	// With no script the page is whole: every scene is laid out complete.
	// Under reduced motion the script only wires the two controls (the
	// preset list and the divider) and the copies' scheme; nothing moves.
	(() => {
		const home = document.querySelector(".docs-home");
		if (!(home instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
		const root = document.documentElement;
		const motion = window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)");
		// The width and height at which a scene is held in view while the
		// page scrolls through it; below it every scene is a column.
		const stage = window.matchMedia("screen and (width >= 64rem) and (height >= 38rem)");
		const clamp = (/** @type {number} */ value) => Math.min(1, Math.max(0, value));
		/** 0 before `from`, 1 after `to`, eased in between. */
		const ramp = (/** @type {number} */ value, /** @type {number} */ from, /** @type {number} */ to) => {
			const t = clamp((value - from) / (to - from));
			return t * t * (3 - 2 * t);
		};
		/** How far the page has scrolled through a scene held in view, 0 to 1. */
		const progressOf = (/** @type {HTMLElement} */ section) => {
			const box = section.getBoundingClientRect();
			const travel = box.height - window.innerHeight;
			return travel > 0 ? clamp(-box.top / travel) : box.top <= 0 ? 1 : 0;
		};

		// --- The story: typed markup, the browser's picture, Cirth's ----------
		const story = home.querySelector("[data-docs-story]");
		const typed = story?.querySelector("[data-docs-story-typed]");
		const source = story?.querySelector("[data-docs-story-code]");
		/** The listing's text pieces, so a prefix of it can be drawn. */
		const pieces = [];
		if (typed instanceof HTMLElement && source instanceof HTMLElement) {
			typed.innerHTML = source.innerHTML;
			const walker = document.createTreeWalker(typed, NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT);
			while (walker.nextNode()) {
				const node = /** @type {Text} */ (walker.currentNode);
				pieces.push({ node, text: node.data });
			}
		}
		const total = pieces.reduce((sum, piece) => sum + piece.text.length, 0);
		let shown = -1;
		const type = (/** @type {number} */ count) => {
			if (count === shown) return;
			shown = count;
			let left = count;
			for (const piece of pieces) {
				const take = Math.max(0, Math.min(piece.text.length, left));
				if (piece.node.data.length !== take) piece.node.data = piece.text.slice(0, take);
				left -= piece.text.length;
			}
		};
		const updateStory = (/** @type {boolean} */ moving) => {
			if (!(story instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
			if (!moving) {
				type(total);
				return;
			}
			const p = progressOf(story);
			// 0 to 30%: the markup is written; to 38%: it stands complete;
			// 38 to 44%: the browser's picture comes up in front of it and
			// stays until 62%; 62 to 70%: it goes and Cirth's takes its
			// place, then holds to the end.
			type(Math.round(total * clamp(p / 0.3)));
			// The browser's picture goes before Cirth's comes, so the two are
			// never on screen half and half.
			const front = ramp(p, 0.38, 0.44);
			const cirth = ramp(p, 0.66, 0.7);
			story.style.setProperty("--docs-front", String(front));
			story.style.setProperty("--docs-browser", String(front * (1 - ramp(p, 0.62, 0.66))));
			story.style.setProperty("--docs-cirth", String(cirth));
			story.style.setProperty("--docs-typing", p < 0.3 ? "1" : "0");
			story.dataset.step = p < 0.38 ? "1" : p < 0.66 ? "2" : "3";
			story.dataset.progress = p.toFixed(3);
		};

		// --- Measured: three facts, one after another -------------------------
		const measured = home.querySelector("[data-docs-measured]");
		const facts = [...(measured?.querySelectorAll("[data-docs-measured-fact]") ?? [])];
		const updateMeasured = (/** @type {boolean} */ moving) => {
			if (!(measured instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
			const p = moving ? progressOf(measured) : 1;
			facts.forEach((fact, index) => {
				if (!(fact instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
				// Each fact owns a third of the scroll and has composed by the
				// middle of it.
				fact.style.setProperty("--docs-fact", moving ? String(ramp(p, index / 3 - 0.05, index / 3 + 0.18)) : "1");
			});
			measured.dataset.step = String(Math.min(3, Math.floor(p * 3) + 1));
			measured.dataset.progress = p.toFixed(3);
		};

		// --- Your theme: one declaration at a time ----------------------------
		const theme = home.querySelector("[data-docs-theme]");
		const themeRoot = theme?.querySelector(".docs-theme-copy")?.shadowRoot ?? null;
		const themeStates = [...(themeRoot?.querySelectorAll("style[data-docs-theme-state]") ?? [])];
		const stateIds = themeStates.map((style) => /** @type {HTMLElement} */ (style).dataset.docsThemeState ?? "");
		let themeState = "";
		const showThemeState = (/** @type {number} */ index) => {
			const id = stateIds[index] ?? "";
			if (!(theme instanceof HTMLElement) || id === themeState) return;
			themeState = id;
			themeStates.forEach((style, at) => {
				if (style instanceof HTMLStyleElement) style.media = at === index ? "all" : "not all";
			});
			// Each token shows the value it has at this state; the one that
			// just changed is marked.
			for (const line of theme.querySelectorAll("[data-docs-theme-token]")) {
				const values = [...line.querySelectorAll("[data-docs-theme-value]")];
				const reached = values.filter((value) => stateIds.indexOf(/** @type {HTMLElement} */ (value).dataset.docsThemeValue ?? "") <= index);
				const current = reached.at(-1) ?? values[0];
				for (const value of values) /** @type {HTMLElement} */ (value).hidden = value !== current;
				line.toggleAttribute("data-changed", index > 0 && current === values.at(-1) && /** @type {HTMLElement} */ (current).dataset.docsThemeValue === id);
			}
			for (const step of theme.querySelectorAll("[data-docs-theme-step]")) {
				const at = stateIds.indexOf(/** @type {HTMLElement} */ (step).dataset.docsThemeStep ?? "");
				step.toggleAttribute("data-current", at === index);
				step.toggleAttribute("data-done", at <= index);
			}
			theme.dataset.state = id;
		};
		const updateTheme = (/** @type {boolean} */ moving) => {
			if (!(theme instanceof HTMLElement) || stateIds.length === 0) return;
			if (!moving) {
				showThemeState(stateIds.length - 1);
				return;
			}
			const p = progressOf(theme);
			// The starting theme, then each change, with the last one held the
			// longest so the finished theme can be read.
			const index = p < 0.18 ? 0 : p < 0.4 ? 1 : p < 0.62 ? 2 : 3;
			showThemeState(Math.min(index, stateIds.length - 1));
			theme.dataset.progress = p.toFixed(3);
		};

		// --- The orbit: turns with the scroll, holds still under a hand -------
		const agnostic = home.querySelector("[data-docs-agnostic]");
		const orbit = agnostic?.querySelector(".docs-agnostic-orbit");
		let held = false;
		if (orbit instanceof HTMLElement) {
			const hold = (/** @type {boolean} */ value) => () => {
				held = value || orbit.matches(":hover") || orbit.matches(":focus-within");
			};
			orbit.addEventListener("pointerenter", hold(true));
			orbit.addEventListener("pointerleave", hold(false));
			orbit.addEventListener("focusin", hold(true));
			orbit.addEventListener("focusout", hold(false));
		}
		const updateOrbit = (/** @type {boolean} */ moving) => {
			if (!(orbit instanceof HTMLElement) || !(agnostic instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
			if (!moving) {
				orbit.style.removeProperty("--docs-orbit");
				return;
			}
			if (held) return;
			const box = agnostic.getBoundingClientRect();
			// From the band's top entering the window to its bottom leaving it.
			const p = clamp((window.innerHeight - box.top) / (window.innerHeight + box.height));
			orbit.style.setProperty("--docs-orbit", `${(p * 32 - 16).toFixed(2)}deg`);
		};

		// --- The field of colour: one layer, carried through the scenes -------
		const aurora = home.querySelector(".docs-aurora");
		// Where each glow is, how large, how strong and how far its hue is
		// turned from the accent, for each scene. The hero's arrangement is
		// the stylesheet's default, so with no script and under reduced
		// motion the field is the hero's.
		/** @type {Record<string, number[]>} */
		const fields = {
			// warm x, y, scale, opacity, hue; cool x, y, scale, opacity, hue; gold x, y, scale, opacity
			hero: [78, 38, 1, 1, 0, 56, 76, 1, 1, -100, 30, 20, 0.6, 0],
			story: [86, 30, 0.8, 0.6, 0, 20, 82, 0.9, 0.7, -100, 50, 50, 0.6, 0],
			measured: [24, 34, 1.05, 0.7, 20, 80, 70, 0.8, 0.55, -120, 60, 90, 0.7, 0.2],
			theme: [70, 22, 0.9, 0.65, 60, 30, 80, 0.85, 0.6, -80, 50, 50, 0.6, 0],
			presets: [18, 70, 0.85, 0.55, -20, 82, 26, 0.9, 0.7, -110, 50, 50, 0.6, 0],
			agnostic: [16, 30, 1.15, 0.9, -40, 44, 84, 1.1, 0.85, -100, 86, 22, 1, 0.9],
			pure: [70, 60, 0.8, 0.4, 0, 30, 40, 0.7, 0.35, -100, 50, 50, 0.6, 0],
		};
		const names = ["warm-x", "warm-y", "warm-s", "warm-o", "warm-h", "cool-x", "cool-y", "cool-s", "cool-o", "cool-h", "gold-x", "gold-y", "gold-s", "gold-o"];
		const scenes = [...home.querySelectorAll("[data-aurora]")];
		const updateAurora = (/** @type {boolean} */ moving) => {
			if (!(aurora instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
			if (!moving) {
				for (const name of names) aurora.style.removeProperty(`--docs-aurora-${name}`);
				return;
			}
			// Anchors: the top of the page for the hero, then the middle of
			// each scene. The window's middle falls between two of them, and
			// the field is that far from one arrangement to the next.
			const middle = window.scrollY + window.innerHeight / 2;
			const anchors = [{ at: window.innerHeight / 2, field: fields.hero }];
			for (const scene of scenes) {
				const box = scene.getBoundingClientRect();
				anchors.push({ at: box.top + window.scrollY + box.height / 2, field: fields[/** @type {HTMLElement} */ (scene).dataset.aurora ?? ""] ?? fields.hero });
			}
			let from = anchors[0];
			let to = anchors[0];
			for (let index = 0; index < anchors.length; index += 1) {
				if (anchors[index].at <= middle) {
					from = anchors[index];
					to = anchors[index + 1] ?? anchors[index];
				}
			}
			const t = to === from ? 0 : ramp(middle, from.at, to.at);
			names.forEach((name, index) => {
				const value = from.field[index] + (to.field[index] - from.field[index]) * t;
				aurora.style.setProperty(`--docs-aurora-${name}`, value.toFixed(3));
			});
		};

		// --- Light arrivals, where scenes are columns -------------------------
		const arrivals = [...home.querySelectorAll("[data-reveal]")];
		const updateArrivals = (/** @type {boolean} */ moving) => {
			const band = window.innerHeight * 0.12;
			for (const element of arrivals) {
				if (!(element instanceof HTMLElement)) continue;
				// Inside a scene held in view, the scene draws itself.
				const staged = stage.matches && element.closest("[data-docs-story], [data-docs-measured], [data-docs-theme]");
				if (!moving || staged) {
					element.style.removeProperty("--docs-arrive");
					continue;
				}
				const top = element.getBoundingClientRect().top;
				element.style.setProperty("--docs-arrive", clamp((window.innerHeight - top) / band).toFixed(3));
			}
		};

		// --- One update, at most once a frame ---------------------------------
		/** @type {Set<Element>} */
		const near = new Set();
		let queued = false;
		const frame = () => {
			queued = false;
			const moving = motion.matches;
			const held = moving && stage.matches;
			home.dataset.motion = moving ? "scroll" : "still";
			home.dataset.stage = held ? "held" : "column";
			updateAurora(moving);
			updateArrivals(moving);
			if (!held || near.has(story)) updateStory(held);
			if (!held || near.has(measured)) updateMeasured(held);
			if (!held || near.has(theme)) updateTheme(held);
			if (near.has(agnostic) || !moving) updateOrbit(held);
		};
		const queue = () => {
			if (queued) return;
			queued = true;
			requestAnimationFrame(frame);
		};
		if ("IntersectionObserver" in window) {
			const watch = new IntersectionObserver(
				(entries) => {
					for (const entry of entries) {
						if (entry.isIntersecting) near.add(entry.target);
						else near.delete(entry.target);
					}
					queue();
				},
				{ rootMargin: "25% 0px" },
			);
			for (const scene of [story, measured, theme, agnostic]) if (scene) watch.observe(scene);
		} else {
			for (const scene of [story, measured, theme, agnostic]) if (scene) near.add(scene);
		}
		window.addEventListener("scroll", queue, { passive: true });
		window.addEventListener("resize", queue, { passive: true });
		window.addEventListener("hashchange", queue);
		window.addEventListener("load", queue, { once: true });
		// A page restored from the back/forward cache is laid out where it was.
		window.addEventListener("pageshow", queue);
		motion.addEventListener("change", queue);
		stage.addEventListener("change", queue);
		frame();

		// --- The copies' scheme follows the page ------------------------------
		// A shadow root does not inherit data-theme, and must not carry it on
		// its host; the theme copy's inner root takes the page's scheme.
		const themeSurface = themeRoot?.querySelector("[data-docs-theme-surface]");
		const follow = () => {
			if (themeSurface instanceof HTMLElement) themeSurface.dataset.theme = root.getAttribute("data-theme") === "dark" ? "dark" : "light";
		};
		follow();
		new MutationObserver(follow).observe(root, { attributeFilter: ["data-theme"] });

		// --- The presets comparator: the divider and the list -----------------
		const compare = home.querySelector("[data-docs-compare]");
		const range = compare?.querySelector("[data-docs-compare-range]");
		if (compare instanceof HTMLElement && range instanceof HTMLInputElement) {
			const describe = (/** @type {number} */ value) =>
				value === 50 ? "Half light, half dark" : value === 0 ? "All dark" : value === 100 ? "All light" : `${value}% light, ${100 - value}% dark`;
			const set = () => {
				const value = Number(range.value);
				compare.style.setProperty("--docs-split", `${value}%`);
				range.setAttribute("aria-valuetext", describe(value));
			};
			range.addEventListener("input", set);
			range.hidden = false;
			set();
		}
		const preset = home.querySelector("[data-docs-compare-preset]");
		if (compare instanceof HTMLElement && preset instanceof HTMLSelectElement) {
			const roots = [...compare.querySelectorAll(".docs-compare-layer")].map((layer) => layer.shadowRoot).filter((shadow) => shadow instanceof ShadowRoot);
			const imports = [...home.querySelectorAll("[data-docs-compare-import]")];
			const apply = () => {
				const name = preset.value;
				for (const shadow of roots) {
					for (const link of shadow.querySelectorAll("link[data-docs-preset]")) {
						if (link instanceof HTMLLinkElement) link.media = link.dataset.docsPreset === name ? "all" : "not all";
					}
				}
				// Every import line is in the document, one on top of the other,
				// so the line's height is the longest one's whichever is shown.
				for (const line of imports) line.toggleAttribute("data-current", /** @type {HTMLElement} */ (line).dataset.docsCompareImport === name);
			};
			preset.addEventListener("change", apply);
			const pick = home.querySelector("[data-docs-compare-pick]");
			if (pick instanceof HTMLElement) pick.hidden = false;
			// A restored page keeps the list's last value; the copies follow it.
			apply();
		}
	})();
</script>
